FROM tomcat:9.0.124-jre8-temurin

COPY target/online-food-delivery.war /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/ROOT.war

EXPOSE 8080

CMD ["catalina.sh", "run"]




  
  kubernetes steps to manage given application:
1. Write the dockerfile in the project directory and start minikube as well
2. Refer above msg for dockerfile template
3. build the image using docker build -t imagename .
4. load the image using, minikube image load imagename
5. create deployment, expose as service with port and target-port set to tomcat server 
6. run the patch command kubectl patch deployment myfoodapp1 -p "{\"spec\":{\"template\":{\"spec\":{\"containers\":[{\"name\":\"foodapp\",\"imagePullPolicy\":\"Never\"}]}}}}"
7. create a tunnel to establish communication between localhost & tomcat kubectl port-forward svc/myfoodapp 6060:8080 where 8080 is the tomcat server & 6060 is the target port where you can see the application running
